.TH SWIFTRLE-CLI 1 "26 October 2026" "1.0.0" "SwiftRLE"
.SH NAME
swiftrle-cli \- bounded PackBits and DICOM RLE frame codec
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swiftrle-cli
encode|decode|inspect|validate|capabilities [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Encodes raw bytes as PackBits, or raw/attached NRRD images as DICOM RLE
frames. Decodes PackBits to raw or DICOM RLE frames to raw/NRRD.
No extension inference occurs. DICOM RLE is not a DICOM dataset.
Inspect validates the frame header against external interpretation;
validate additionally decodes the complete payload.
.SH OPTIONS
.B -i, --input PATH; -o, --output PATH
Select endpoints. A dash denotes stdin/stdout.
.PP
.B --input-format; --output-format
Explicit raw, packbits, dicom-rle-frame or nrrd.
.PP
.B --decoded-bytes N
Mandatory for PackBits decode/inspect/validate. Optional --row-bytes N and
--rows N constrain packets; their product must agree with decoded bytes.
.PP
.B --width; --height; --storage-bits; --meaningful-bits; --sample-type;
.B --components; --colour; --byte-order; --planar-configuration
Mandatory external DICOM frame interpretation and requested raw layout.
Storage bits: 8 or 16; meaningful bits: 1 through storage bits;
sample type: unsigned or signed; components: 1 or 3;
colour: greyscale, rgb, palette or ybr-full;
byte order: little or big; planar configuration: 0 or 1.
Optional --row-bytes includes padding. These are not RLE header fields.
.PP
.B --mode lossless
Only lossless is supported. Quality/max-error are rejected.
.PP
.B --backend automatic|scalar|scalar-cpu|preferred-accelerated|required-accelerated
Scalar is available; preferred acceleration reports fallback;
required acceleration fails with exit 4.
.PP
.B --copy-policy require-sharing|allow-copy
Common storage policy, default require-sharing.
.PP
.B --threads N; --max-memory BYTES; --timeout SECONDS
Positive limits. Defaults: 2 workers, 1073741824 bytes, 120 seconds.
Timeout maximum: 120. The CLI conservatively reserves retained input,
payload/owner/output buffers and I/O workspace before codec admission;
individual input/decoded/compressed buffers are limited to approximately
one eighth of the process budget. Budgets below 65536 bytes fail.
.PP
.B --overwrite
Atomically replace final output. Default publication refuses overwrite,
including a competing creator. Incomplete sibling transactions are removed.
.PP
.B --json; --quiet, -q
JSON inspection/capabilities use stdout. Encode/decode reports use stderr.
Quiet suppresses optional diagnostics, never errors or requested output.
.PP
.B -v; -vv through -vvvvv; --verbose LEVEL; --verbose=LEVEL;
.B -verbose: LEVEL; -verbose:LEVEL
Explicit levels 1 through 5 or plus strings + through +++++.
Bare --verbose/-verbose increments. Forms apply in argument order.
Default 0. Quiet conflicts with verbosity. Levels cumulatively add
summary, stages, configuration, timing and bounded trace. Diagnostics
exclude paths, payload, private metadata and addresses.
.PP
.B -h, --help; help [command]; --version; version
Help/version aliases. No arguments show help.
.SH NRRD PROFILE
Attached ASCII header with LF/CRLF, at most 16384 header bytes,
64 lines, 1024 bytes per line; raw 2D unsigned full16 greyscale payload,
explicit endian and fastest width axis. Extra semantic fields, detached
references, compressed/ASCII payload, skip offsets and 12-in-16 output
are unsupported. Duplicate fields and sizes before dimension are malformed.
.SH STREAMS
Binary stdout contains only payload. Slow I/O uses bounded backpressure
and checks cancellation/deadline. Failure may leave partial stdout;
stdout cannot be rolled back. SIGINT/SIGTERM cancel. File output is final
output only, with no decoded intermediate image files.
.SH EXAMPLES
For payload.bin containing exactly 4096 bytes:
.PP
.nf
swiftrle-cli encode -i payload.bin --input-format raw --output-format packbits -o payload.packbits
swiftrle-cli decode -i payload.packbits --input-format packbits --decoded-bytes 4096 --output-format raw -o restored.bin
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 arguments; 3 malformed; 4 unsupported format/feature/layout/backend;
5 resource limit/deadline; 6 I/O/storage including broken pipe; 7 internal;
130 cancellation. Broken pipe never reports success.
.SH INSTALLATION
Scripts/install-cli.sh stages binary and matching manual using absolute
PREFIX and optional DESTDIR. The first argument selects the prebuilt binary.
